From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 11:52:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] script: Treat any defined detail as present in
 performance.measure

The check for a non-empty PerformanceMeasureOptions only counted a
`detail` that is an object or null, so `{detail: 0}` or `{detail: false}`
didn't throw. A string only did because mozjs's `is_object_or_null`
returns true for strings.

Fork note: meant for upstream; found with the QuickJS backend, whose
is_object_or_null() is false for strings. Drop once upstream has it.

Testing: Extends user-timing/measure_exception.html.

Validation: Release builds of this stack (QuickJS through the QuickJS workflow's patch step, servo-quickjs 0605066) with `./mach test-wpt --processes 4` of html/webappapis/microtask-queuing, user-timing and /_mozilla/mozilla/media-query-list-gc-listener.html (72 tests): all as expected with QuickJS; with SpiderMonkey all as expected except an unexpected PASS of a subtest of measure_associated_with_navigation_timing.html that compares a sum of measure durations, without measure options.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; root-caused, written and tested by the agent)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 components/script/dom/performance/performance.rs   | 2 +-
 tests/wpt/meta/MANIFEST.json                       | 2 +-
 tests/wpt/tests/user-timing/measure_exception.html | 1 +
 3 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/components/script/dom/performance/performance.rs b/components/script/dom/performance/performance.rs
index 0f9ed1accdb..fdf03a377b3 100644
--- a/components/script/dom/performance/performance.rs
+++ b/components/script/dom/performance/performance.rs
@@ -632,7 +632,7 @@ impl PerformanceMethods<crate::DomTypeHolder> for Performance {
             (options.start.is_some() ||
                 options.duration.is_some() ||
                 options.end.is_some() ||
-                options.detail.get().is_object_or_null())
+                !options.detail.get().is_undefined())
         {
             // Step 1.1 If endMark is given, throw a TypeError.
             if end_mark.is_some() {
diff --git a/tests/wpt/meta/MANIFEST.json b/tests/wpt/meta/MANIFEST.json
index 2720eb87c14..2cb6e69ddcf 100644
--- a/tests/wpt/meta/MANIFEST.json
+++ b/tests/wpt/meta/MANIFEST.json
@@ -1416258,7 +1416258,7 @@
      ]
     ],
     "measure_exception.html": [
-     "5c1aa086c0fc882e4dd3c10ee2da637ead46b373",
+     "ed5ed8ef713acc51d4bacee9e9c51d36ce407f5b",
      [
       null,
       {}
diff --git a/tests/wpt/tests/user-timing/measure_exception.html b/tests/wpt/tests/user-timing/measure_exception.html
index 5c1aa086c0f..ed5ed8ef713 100644
--- a/tests/wpt/tests/user-timing/measure_exception.html
+++ b/tests/wpt/tests/user-timing/measure_exception.html
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@ test_method_throw_exception('performance.measure("Exception6", "NonExistMark1",
 test_method_throw_exception('performance.measure("Exception7", "redirectStart")', 'INVALID_ACCESS_ERR');
 test_method_throw_exception('performance.measure("Exception8", {"detail": "non-empty"})', TypeError);
 test_method_throw_exception('performance.measure("Exception9", {"start": 1, "duration": 2, "end": 3})', TypeError);
+test_method_throw_exception('performance.measure("Exception10", {"detail": 0})', TypeError);
 </script>
 </body>
 </html>
